              "Configuring DHCP relay agent information option (Option 82)", pp20-22;
            - AW+ CLI pages ip-dhcp-relay-agent-option, -remote-id, -checking and
              ip-dhcp-relay-information-policy.
          Option 82 is inserted by the DHCP RELAY, so the DUT was tested as a relay.
          8 steps as executed, plus a baseline.
Build:    swi_d  sin_x96056-20261012-24  (flash:/x960-tb277.rel, build date Mon Oct 12 2026)
          AT-x960-56YSQ, S/N A2WQS700B, standalone Active Master, console u2 @115200
Configs:  swi_d.cfg (running-config after setup; saved to startup: no)

VERDICT: PASS -- the relay's Option 82 handling is correct on every graded limb:
insertion, the two sub-option contents, the configurable remote-id and its revert, all
four information-policy actions, response-path checking, the strip on the way back to
the client, and survival of a reboot.
      baseline, insertion disabled ......... option 82 ABSENT in all 3 relayed DISCOVERs
      insertion enabled .................... circuit-id "vlan10", remote-id = switch MAC
      circuit-id ........................... "vlan10", the ISC default, no CLI to change it
      remote-id default .................... 00 06 e0 1a ea d4 70 43 (type 0, the switch MAC)
      remote-id configured ................. 01 0c "CK-REMOTE-82" (type 1, ASCII, len 12)
      remote-id no-form .................... back to the switch MAC, proven on the wire
      remote-id refused while agent-option off  "% Can not configure DHCP Relay agent
                                                option remote-id unless agent option is set"
      information policy replace (default) . 1 TLV, the DUT's own
      information policy keep .............. 1 TLV, the client's, untouched
      information policy append ............ 2 TLVs, the client's first then the DUT's
      information policy drop .............. 0 relayed, offers 0/3
      agent-option checking, matched reply . 3 of 3 OFFERs delivered to the client
      agent-option checking, bogus reply ... 0 of 3 OFFERs delivered to the client
      option 82 in the reply to the client . stripped in every leg (RFC 3046)
      reboot ............................... insertion, remote-id, policy and server all survive
CAVEAT:  The circuit-id has no CLI on this platform, so only its default ("vlan10") is
         covered. The remote-id was exercised with one ASCII string. Response-path
         checking was exercised with BOTH sub-options wrong at once, so per-sub-option
         matching is not separated. One relay interface on an untagged access VLAN,
         one configured server, IPv4 only.

