STEP 4 -- `agent-option checking` validates SERVER RESPONSES
          (legs `checking-on-no-opt82`, `chk-on-bogus-resp`, `checking-on-with-opt82`)  PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The AW+ command reference defines the direction: the command "enables the DHCP Relay
  Agent to check DHCP Relay Agent Information Option (Option 82) information in RESPONSE
  PACKETS RETURNED FROM DHCP SERVERS. If the information does not match the information
  it has for its own client (downstream) interface then the DHCP Relay Agent drops the
  packet." Client-originated option 82 is governed by `ip dhcp-relay information policy`
  instead, and is STEP 5.

